    /// (D16, #2406), by a variant call's callee or a struct literal: the
    /// emitter writes `Boxed::placed` there (`check_core_place_boxes`).
    pub placed_in_block: collections::BTreeSet[i64],
    /// **The lists of views a `let` binds what they may view after** (#490),
    /// by the `let`'s start, with whether the list's `let` said `mut`: the
    /// emitter binds each list again right after it, so the list is dropped
    /// before what it views (`check_core_view_list_rebound`).
    pub view_list_rebinds: collections::BTreeMap[i64, Vec[(String, bool)]],
    /// The `let`s of the lists `view_list_rebinds` binds again, by the
    /// `let`'s start: a `let mut` there may change nothing before.
    pub view_list_rebound: collections::BTreeSet[i64],
    pub counted: collections::BTreeSet[i64],
    pub lent_bindings: collections::BTreeMap[i64, collections::BTreeSet[String]],
    /// **The parts an arm keeps in place out of a field of a `mut`
    /// parameter**, by the arm's body (#1139): `match h.node` binds them
    /// `ref mut`, so the arm changes the part where it is.
    pub in_place_bindings: collections::BTreeMap[i64, collections::BTreeSet[String]],
    pub taking_arms: collections::BTreeMap[i64, String],
    /// **A part taken out of a `mut` parameter or a `let mut` view** to be
